---
import CourseHome from '../../../../components/course/CourseHome.astro';
import { DATA_MODELLING } from '../../../../courses/data-modelling/syllabus';
import '../../../../styles/lesson-kit.css';
---
<CourseHome course={DATA_MODELLING}>
  <p class="cs-meta"><strong>Quick reference:</strong> <a href="/learn/courses/data-modelling/glossary/">glossary</a> · <a href="/learn/courses/data-modelling/cheat-sheet/">cheat sheet</a> · <a href="/learn/courses/sql/sandbox/">SQL sandbox</a></p>
  <section class="cs-builds">
    <h2>What you will be able to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Design a star schema</strong> from a business process: choose the grain, the facts and the dimensions, and plan a whole warehouse with a bus matrix.</li>
      <li><strong>Handle history</strong> with slowly changing dimensions, and answer "as it was then" questions correctly.</li>
      <li><strong>Know the other approaches</strong>: normal forms, Inmon, Data Vault, one big table and the lakehouse, and when each fits.</li>
      <li><strong>Load and test a warehouse</strong>: staging layers, MERGE, audit columns and tests for keys and orphans.</li>
      <li><strong>Leave with a portfolio project</strong>: the Northbay warehouse, designed, built and tested by you, then moved to a cloud warehouse.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Every lesson has diagrams, live SQL boxes where you build each piece in your browser, and a 3-question quiz. Know basic SQL first: <a href="/learn/courses/sql/">SQL for analysts</a>, Modules 1-4. For the tools that run warehouses in production (dbt, Dagster, Azure SQL), go on to <a href="/learn/courses/etl/">Pipeline to Dashboard</a>.</p>
  </section>
</CourseHome>
